From 8a491bf2a09683e4ef79f3e0e56e5e727f35d842 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mytochondria audit <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 15:44:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Condition sample/permute/adaptive GSEA p-values on the sign
 of the permutation ES

gsea(method = "sample" | "permute") and adaptive = TRUE divided the number of
permutations at least as extreme as the observed ES by the total number of
permutations. GSEA (Subramanian et al. 2005), fgsea, DOSE and enrichit's own
multilevel method use the permutations whose ES has the same sign as the
observed one, so these p-values were about half of the multilevel ones for the
same gene set (exact enumeration on 24 genes / sets of 3: 0.45 vs 0.88).

The observed ES on the "sample" path is now compared through the same sparse
routine that scores the permutations, so a set lying entirely at one end of the
list (ES = +/-1) is no longer reported at the permutation floor.

Adds a regression test against an exact enumeration and a NEWS entry.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TaHntBDKuZJpMAAMenkC44
